SUMMARY:StockAI: verify K-Score tuner ran on clean data
DESCRIPTION:The only item with a real deadline. tune_kscore_weights runs Su
 nday 14:00 PT - this is its first run since the fabricated rs_score rows w
 ere nulled (1915 rows) and the corrupted weight override cleared.\n\n1) WE
 IGHT OVERRIDE\ndocker exec stockai-redis-1 redis-cli GET stockai:kscore_we
 ights\nPASS: empty, or relative_strength at/near 0.10 (empty = no override
 , default applies).\nREGRESSION: relative_strength back near 0.05 - the tu
 ner re-learned from placeholder data. Check _rs_score()'s fail direction f
 irst; it must return (None, None), never (50.0, 1.0).\n\n2) NEW HK ROWS NO
 T REVERTING\nSELECT s.market, COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE r.rs_score = 50.0) AS
  placeholder, COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE r.rs_score IS NULL) AS excluded, COUN
 T(*) FILTER (WHERE r.rs_score IS NOT NULL) AS real_scores FROM rankings r 
 JOIN stocks s ON s.id = r.stock_id WHERE r.as_of >= CURRENT_DATE - 7 GROUP
  BY 1;\nPASS: HK placeholder at/near 0 and real_scores growing (baseline w
 as 915).\n\n3) HK BENCHMARK STILL FRESH\n2800.HK is active=false so only t
 he HK refresh job feeds it - exactly how XLP went 102 days stale unnoticed
 .\nSELECT s.symbol, MAX(p.ts)::date AS newest, (CURRENT_DATE - MAX(p.ts)::
 date) AS age_days FROM stocks s JOIN prices p ON p.stock_id = s.id WHERE s
 .symbol IN ('2800.HK','XLP','XLK','SPY') GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 3 DESC;\nPASS
 : all four within ~4 days of each other (guard rejects >10 days).\n\nALSO:
  rebuild backend images with docker compose build on the next deploy windo
 w - shared/common/market_calendar.py currently lives in containers via doc
 ker cp and reverts on any container recreation.\n\nFull checklist: https:/
 /claude.ai/code/artifact/f2462c2d-bde6-4f30-99d9-121ede27f411
