SUMMARY:StockAI: quarterly structural checks
DESCRIPTION:Longer-horizon items where a quarter of accumulated data change
 s the answer, plus two guards written 2026-09-08 that are designed to fire
  on a schedule you will not be watching.\n\n1) DID ANY DIGEST FIRE ON A MA
 RKET HOLIDAY?\nUS markets closed Thanksgiving 2026-11-26 and Christmas 202
 6-12-25 - both weekdays, both in-window. The real test of the new holiday 
 gate.\ndocker logs stockai-market-data-1 --since 720h 2>&1 | grep -E "dige
 st.done|brief.done|digest_skip_market_closed" | grep "2026-11-26"\nPASS: d
 igest_skip_market_closed entries and ZERO digest.done for that date.\nNOTE
 : HK should STILL send on a US-only holiday - the filter is per-market by 
 design.\n\n2) 2027 HOLIDAY CALENDAR (hard deadline 2027-01-01)\nassert_cal
 endar_coverage() is built to fail in October of the final covered year, so
  tests should start failing on their own and force the extension.\ncd serv
 ices/market-data && python -m pytest tests/test_aud_digest_holiday_and_cal
 endar.py -q\nDO: reconcile the HK 2027 LUNAR dates against HKEX's publishe
 d notice - they are marked PROVISIONAL in the source because Lunar New Yea
 r, Ching Ming, Buddha's Birthday, Tuen Ng, Mid-Autumn and Chung Yeung cann
 ot be derived from any weekday rule. They are a reconstruction, not a tran
 scription.\nWATCH: if tests still pass in Oct 2027 the coverage assertion 
 is not wired into the run - a guard that exists but never fires is exactly
  what it was written to prevent.\n\n3) ML SMALL-SAMPLE - THE ONLY LEVER LE
 FT\nBinding constraint is n_test ~= 31 rows, which produces the extreme 0.
 0/1.0 AUCs and the 89% suppression rate.\nDO: backfill price history (~667
  bars is only 2.6 years; the 5-year lookback is already requested, the dat
 a is simply absent), and A/B the dead-zone filter on cv_auc - never on tes
 t AUC, which is noise at n=31.\nDO NOT: run a fleet-wide retrain. 89% of f
 reshly retrained models immediately self-suppress and stale models measure
  marginally BETTER than fresh. The lever is data, not scheduling.\n\n4) AD
 VANCED-TIER GUARD (currently latent)\nThe nav/page guard mismatch is fixed
  but its dead-link half never activated in prod - only an ADMIN/BASIC and 
 a USER/BASIC account exist. If anyone is set to ADVANCED, walk the Learnin
 g section and confirm all 9 items open rather than bouncing to the dashboa
 rd.\ncd frontend && npx vitest run src/lib/navGuardParity.test.ts  (81 tes
 ts)\n\nDO NOT RE-DERIVE THESE AS FINDINGS:\n- Stop execution compares agai
 nst current_stop, not the original stop_loss. Correct as written.\n- HK GR
 OWTH holding more cash than initial capital: it is simply profitable.\n- P
 rebreakout's 0% win rate: effective sample ~2-3.\n- Confidence being "mean
 ingless": the inversion was AUD232-BUY-FROM-TOP, fixed 2026-08-03; post-fi
 x it is correctly signed. Do not rebuild the formula.\n- Ingestion being b
 roken: it is the healthiest domain audited - 123,475 bars, zero duplicates
 , zero high<low, zero out-of-range closes.\n- Alert dedup/cooldown/suppres
 sion and research-engine LLM cost: both surveyed clean 2026-09-08.\n- Thre
 shold retuning of any alert: every looser variant measured worse.\n\nFull 
 checklist: https://claude.ai/code/artifact/f2462c2d-bde6-4f30-99d9-121ede2
 7f411
